course: dictionary
lesson: 10678
title: Unopened and still sealed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Un- at the start of a word often means not. Open means to undo or lift something so you can see inside, so unopened means not opened yet, still closed or sealed. You can check this by taking off the un- and seeing if the word still fits: «opened» makes sense in the same place.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Lily's dad writes a long sorry letter to his brother after ten years; it comes back unopened.» The letter has been sent and returned, and nobody has read it, so unopened means the envelope was never opened.
explain: Stories use unopened things to build mystery. An unopened box or letter makes the reader wonder what is inside. Ask yourself what the character does not know yet, and the word will give you a clue about the plot.
fact: Un- often means not, so unopened means not opened.
fact: «Unopened» means not opened yet; still closed or sealed.
fact: An unopened letter has not been read.
fact: Unopened food and medicine often stay fresh longer, because they are still sealed.
fact: Phrases to remember: «unopened letter», «unopened packet», «left unopened».
exercise: «Lily's dad writes a long sorry letter to his brother after ten years; it comes back unopened.» What does unopened mean here? | Read many times and loved | Sent to the wrong town | Torn into small pieces | *Not opened yet, still sealed
exercise: Which word means the opposite of unopened? | *opened | closed | packet | sealed
exercise: Why would a story use an unopened box? | It means the box is broken | *It builds mystery, because we do not know what is inside | It shows the box is very old | It is always empty
test:
«She left the packet unopened on the kitchen table.» What does unopened mean? | *Still closed, not opened yet | Opened and empty | Lost under the table | Very heavy
Ella says unopened food stays fresh longer. Why? | It has already been eaten | *It is still sealed and has not been opened | It is too old to eat | It goes bad faster than opened food
exam:
Jayden finds «an unopened letter» in the post. What does unopened tell him? | It was written by his teacher | *It has not been read yet | It has been read twice | It is a letter from a shop
